  <text>
      <body>
         <entry xml:id="elogin-dlgenr"
            xml:lang="en"
            type="mainEntry"
            prev="#"
            next="#"
            source="Genesis Rabbah">
            <form type="lemma" opt="false">
               <orth type="lemma" xml:lang="jpa" opt="false" select="true">אילוגין</orth>
               <orth type="transliteration" xml:lang="fjb" opt="false">ʾylwgyn</orth>
               <pron notation="rabbinic" opt="false">elogin</pron>
               <gramGrp opt="false">
                  <gram type="pos" opt="false">noun</gram>
                  <gram type="gen" opt="false">m.</gram>
               </gramGrp>
            </form>
            <sense xml:id="elogin-dlgenr-1">
               <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en" subtype="sense">
                  <quote>record (record of sins), accusation, sentence</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="translationEquivalent" xml:lang="grc">
                  <quote>ἐλόγιον</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="example" xml:lang="jpa">
                  <quote>אין הקב"ה 
                     <app>
                        <lem>פורע</lem>
                        <rdg wit="#K V Ox1 Ox2">נפרע</rdg>
                     </app> מן האומות עד שהוא קורא 
                     <app>
                        <lem>אנאלגין</lem>
                        <rdg wit="#K V Ox1">אגאליגין</rdg>
                        <rdg wit="#Ox2">אגליגין</rdg>
                        <rdg wit="#Vat2">אנאליגין</rdg>
                     </app></quote>
                  <bibl>
                     <ref type="witness">28,1</ref>
                     <ref type="witness">I 259: [notes]</ref>
                  </bibl>
                  <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en">
                     <quote>The Holy One, blessed be He, does not punish the nations until he reads to them the record of sin ...</quote>
                  </cit>
                  <note>= <bibl type="ancient">Yalq Hi 920 [509b: 10]</bibl> (<term xml:lang="jpa">אולוגין</term>)</note>
               </cit>
            </sense>
            <note>See MY. Cf. <bibl type="modern">AC I 88ab</bibl>; <bibl type="modern">Jastrow I 49a</bibl>; <bibl type="modern">Levy I 64b</bibl>. The spelling in GenR is probably corrupted. <bibl type="modern">Lieberman (1944) 29 (n. 182)</bibl> suggests for <bibl type="ancient">PRK 159b</bibl> <term xml:lang="jpa">אנגלין</term> Gr. <term xml:lang="grc">ἐνλογεῖον</term>, <term xml:lang="grc">ἐλλογεῖον</term> “imputatio“, which may fit also the reading in GenR.</note>
            <ref type="bibliography">
               <bibl>
                  <title>Krauss, LW II</title>
                  <citedRange>33b-34a</citedRange>
               </bibl>
            </ref>
         </entry>
      </body>
